  "doc": "M3-C04-02 greybox: ch04/haluna_wake, Haluna on the Pilgrim's Wake night (act1_ch04.md C4-01 to C4-08), a stand-in for ch02/haluna's night variant: HalunaStory is not data-driven (ADR 0035), so Ch4's night is its own zone until Haluna moves to ZoneStory, and env-art's wake-night dressing (M3-C04-03) lands on the real Haluna. Layout, north is -z: Neme's house and door (south), the lane north past dark houses (four lit windows that go dark once the lamps leave), the shut market and the closed inn (west), the chapel court (east), the dock running east into the sea (no lamps, the sea-glow only), and the causeway head (north) with the wake-shell wall, its gap and Imra's shell, the lamps on its top, the four feast tables, and the causeway's dark line beyond it under the tide. states (Ch04Zone): the windows dark from ch04_started; Asha's shell in the wall from ch04_shell_set; the village gone home, the wall's lamps low and the stranger kneeling at the wall from ch04_dock_comforted; gone again from ch04_saw_ysolde_ink. The sea is a solid floor 1.2 m down behind rails: there is no swimming in the greybox.",
